{"skill":{"slug":"edge-tts","displayName":"Edge TTS"},"version":{"version":"2.0.0","createdAt":1769456031010,"changelog":"**Major upgrade with added scripts, configurability, and streamlined TTS triggers**\n\n- Added Node.js scripts for TTS conversion and config management (`tts-converter.js`, `config-manager.js`), with installation and usage instructions.\n- Added resource and reference files, including a complete voice/option guide and install script.\n- Changed TTS intent detection to trigger only on the \"tts\" keyword (removes long trigger phrase lists), and clarified keyword filtering prior to conversion.\n- Expanded documentation with workflow, usage examples, advanced configuration, troubleshooting, and testing instructions.\n- Clarified default voice, output formats, temporary file handling, and recommended voice test site.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"skill-info.json","size":580,"sha256":"9ff7416cedf34d589d7b0c9d707ea544e8a3b53b0b0ff64b3adf782bd31b686f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7267,"sha256":"f313dd928f5cfb7d0b0fb477c77fd17beabccd97ee8240649fc711097f978752","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"DISTRIBUTION.md","size":2182,"sha256":"6891c442c5d10f4dc57c6f6586b729cb306e9e797b2cf97b2fdcf40eed933342","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"install.sh","size":449,"sha256":"4dada8f2086afefabfc047f3d9ff3d35bfbc964e8203cf1a3e73ff5cc96762ac","contentType":"application/x-shellscript"},{"path":"scripts/tts-converter.js","size":8370,"sha256":"3c01a4816738428bf9c4ffb56aec6f4ba766200a1f5a54ed2299ffec1cfaafbf","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/package-lock.json","size":9718,"sha256":"7badc62afe2cdfc7d74eb4cb93e8dbf2c5fe2543b1628e8579bcbbbe8936a8f0","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/package.json","size":548,"sha256":"35f4b0da40526a5f86f4342bdd0c36f810468370e160dde39caa992b37789e12","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/config-manager.js","size":7957,"sha256":"f085b8642039e4c9ad37b8e8f0933979657de9d1253fad47509428f5659bf8ca","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"references/node_edge_tts_guide.md","size":6099,"sha256":"e2fd9644e658fc4e3bf1ab7fda766c7d870cf76ac2f4327a023fe77321953cc2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2189,"sha256":"8c0ce145a61368707db1d200b15c862cd0e1f8ae6d3b6fada37c668ac34c62d6","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789017655769,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b667fc7d796d9539bdebeb08c87862b64346aa32208375a6cb801d0b934d2579","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b667fc7d796d9539bdebeb08c87862b64346aa32208375a6cb801d0b934d2579","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: edge-tts\nVersion: 2.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw Edge-TTS skill is designed for text-to-speech conversion using the `node-edge-tts` npm package. All analyzed files, including `SKILL.md`, `install.sh`, `tts-converter.js`, and `config-manager.js`, demonstrate behavior strictly aligned with this stated purpose. File system operations are limited to creating temporary audio files in the system's temp directory and managing a user-specific configuration file (`~/.tts-config.json`). Network access is solely for connecting to the legitimate Microsoft Edge TTS service. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent to perform unauthorized actions. The skill's capabilities are appropriate for its function.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159896553},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789017655769},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This appears to be a real text-to-speech skill, but it needs review because its helper scripts can write or delete arbitrary user-writable files when given unsafe paths and it sends text to an online TTS service.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The converter accepts arbitrary output paths without containment or overwrite checks, and temporary audio/subtitle files are kept in a shared predictable temp directory with no automatic cleanup.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation runs npm install for registry dependencies, package.json uses semver ranges, package-lock resolves ws 8.19.0, and documentation plus npm test include unpinned npx examples.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Activation guidance relies on a broad 'tts' keyword and 'triggers or user request' language, which could cause unintended conversion of text and transmission to the online TTS service.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent preferences in ~/.tts-config.json are disclosed and purpose-aligned, but --config-path is unrestricted and --reset unlinks that path while suppressing deletion errors.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifacts coherently implement Edge TTS conversion, voice options, subtitles, and preference management; the config manager is disclosed in SKILL.md and is purpose-related.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending TTS text to Microsoft's online service and running npm dependencies. Avoid using this skill on sensitive text, avoid unpinned npx examples, keep output paths in a dedicated folder, and do not use custom --config-path or --reset unless you have checked the target path.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the package includes an actual TTS converter, and SKILL.md discloses the configuration manager and its persistent settings, so this is not evidence of tool poisoning.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Accepted as a scoping concern: a plain 'tts' keyword trigger is broader than needed for a service that sends text online and creates files.\n[SQP-2] expected: Online Microsoft Edge TTS use is disclosed, but the user-facing privacy warning about sending submitted text to a third party is not prominent.\n[RP1] unexpected: Accepted as supply-chain guidance: several examples and the npm test script use unpinned npx execution, which is avoidable.\n[SC1] unexpected: Partially accepted: package-lock.json pins resolved versions, but package.json still uses caret ranges and install guidance relies on npm install.\n[SC4] unexpected: Accepted as a dependency risk based on the local lockfile resolving ws 8.19.0 and the supplied advisory context; this is not malicious by itself.\n[SDI-1] expected: Downgraded: keyword filtering changes user text, but the behavior is disclosed in SKILL.md and logged by the script; users should know exact rendering is not guaranteed by default.\n[EA2] expected: Overridden: the cited text says temporary files are not automatically deleted; I did not find automatic destructive cleanup in the converter.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: the default en-US voice and language are disclosed and configurable, so this is a usability/default-locale issue rather than a material security concern.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as material Review evidence: scripts/tts-converter.js passes --output directly to the TTS writer without restricting location or preventing overwrite.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted with local-attack limits: temporary output uses a predictable shared directory and retained files, which can expose generated audio or subtitles on shared systems.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as material Review evidence: scripts/config-manager.js allows --config-path with --reset to unlink an arbitrary user-writable file and hides unlink errors.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789017655769}}}}}